/-! Empty type and proof-relevant conjunction (PART 3.5 of the foundation).

Model unit `foundation_empty_and` — moved out of `crates/clean-verify/src/spec/core_spec/foundation_types.rs`
(embed memo W1). Registered by `Specification::register_model_unit(ModelUnit::FoundationEmptyAnd)`
through the same `add_inductive` / `add_recursive_def` path the literals used; the
fidelity oracle in `spec/model_units/tests.rs` pins this file against the retained
literal. EVERY declaration must carry a `/-- ... -/` doc comment: its text is the
registered description, byte for byte. -/

/-- Uninhabited type. Used for constructor discrimination via large elimination. -/
inductive Empty : Type

-- =========================================================
-- PART 3.5: Conjunction (AndType) type
-- =========================================================
-- AndType is a proof-relevant conjunction used in bidirectional proofs.

-- AndType type (proof-relevant conjunction)
/-- Proof-relevant conjunction: AndType A B holds when both A and B hold. -/
inductive AndType (A : Type) (B : Type) : Type
| intro : A → B → AndType A B
